  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Dry and warm conditions continue to \ndominate in the short term as a dry pattern remains over the \nforecast area. High temperatures both this afternoon and Tuesday \nafternoon are expected to be in the 60s and 70s. Overnight lows \ntonight and Tuesday night will be in the 30s and 40s.\n\nAll models are depicting an upper level low pressure system diving\nto the south from the Pacific Northwest states to just off the coast \nof Western California late Tuesday. Light valley rain showers and \nmountain snow showers are expected to develop during the latter \nportion of the afternoon and overnight period. Winds will be breezy \nto locally windy with gusts of 25 to 40 mph. Highs will be several \ndegrees cooler with readings in the 50s and 60s. Overnight lows will \nbe in the 30s and 40s.\n\nA slow forward progression is in store for this storm system as it \ntries to move east across Northern and Central Nevada Wednesday and \nThursday. Valley rain showers and mountain snow showers are again \npossible both days. The estimated three day forecast amounts for \nprecipitation and snowfall are coming in around one-half to two-\nthirds of an inch of rainfall in the valleys with one to four inches \nof snow across the highest elevations in the mountains. Afternoon \nhighs both of these days will be in the 50s and 60s with overnight \nlows in the 30s and 40s.\n\nThe system may be exiting east by the latter portions of the \nweek. Highs will remain on the cool side with readings in the 50s \nand 60s and lows in the 30s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the\nshort term grids as NBM is handling the forecast well. Confidence in \nthe forecast remains high today. Confidence continues to be moderate \nwith respect to the precipitation and temperature forecast Tuesday \nthrough Friday. Low confidence on the chances of a cold front late \nin the week.",
